      "claim": "The preference for better-corroborated theories is defensible on Popper's terms as a pragmatic rule of action based on verisimilitude, not induction. It survives by redefining rationality as adherence to the method of error elimination rather than the pursuit of probable truth, costing us the comfort of believing our best theories are likely true.",
